          %h2#overview Overview
          %p
            The
            %strong Association of Collaborators of Nicolas Bourbaki
            (
            %em> l'Association des collaborateurs de Nicolas Bourbaki
            ) is a collective of mathematicians based in France, who in the 20th century set a standard for a structural and abstract approach to exposition of pure mathematics. They published a series “Elements of mathematics” of 10 multi-volume monographs under the pseudonym ‘Nicolas Bourbaki’, consolidating known results. They also held —and still hold— a largely independent seminar on contemporary research.
          %p
            The members of the group at any one time are required to be under 50 years of age, which is considered the only fixed rule of the group
            %sup#fnref:1>
              %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
            ; the membership is taken under acceptance of an invitation by existing members.
          %p A bit of history can be found at:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicolas_Bourbaki"}> en.wikipedia
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicolas_Bourbaki"}> fr.wikipedia
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://www.britannica.com/EBchecked/topic/75700/Nicolas-Bourbaki"} britannica
          %p and references therein.
          %p
            According to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Dieudonn%C3%A9"} Jean Dieudonné
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+theory"} Lie theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebras"} Lie algebras
            = succeed "&rbrack;." do
              %a{:href => "#Dieudonne"} Dieudonné
          %p Bourbaki has been blamed for following too formal an approach. Indeed, the books are void of much motivation and application, apart from a few of introductions and few chapters on history.
          %p
            Apart from the Bourbaki volumes, there is also a lively
            %em Bourbaki seminar
            which takes place in Paris on certain Saturdays, is open to public and has non-Bourbaki members as invited speakers who present and discuss topics, chosen in advance, of recent development in mathematics. The expositions are subsequently published.
          %h2#SelectedWritings Selected writings
          %p
            On
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+topology"} general topology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+structures"} uniform structures
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groups"} topological groups
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            with some
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+analysis"} real analysis
          %ul
            %li#Bourbaki71
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Bourbaki"}> Nicolas Bourbaki
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em General topology
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-61701-0"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-61701-0
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"} Lie groups
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebras"} Lie algebras
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Bourbaki"}> Nicolas Bourbaki
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lie groups and Lie algebras – Chapters 1-3
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/9783540642428"} ISBN:9783540642428
          %p
            On
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+spaces"} topological vector spaces
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Bourbaki"}> Nicolas Bourbaki
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological Vector Spaces
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-61715-7"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-61715-7
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"}> groupoids
            ,
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoids"} fundamental groupoids
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Bourbaki"}> Nicolas Bourbaki
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topologie Algébrique
              = succeed "," do
